# SYNOPSIS

```usage
PREFS_AREA=area preferences
```

# DESCRIPTION

`preferences` is a preference app, after Be's: a small window for one area of settings(2), not one app with panes.
Each area has a manifest of its own, which names the area in `PREFS_AREA` and makes the program an `app` with `preferences` (manifest(6)), so launcher(8) lists it and deskbar(4) puts it in its Preferences submenu.
The areas are:

: Appearance
  `Appearance:Theme`, a button a theme; `Appearance:HighContrast`, On or Off; `Appearance:Accent`, the theme's own accent or its cool or warm one.
  radharc(4) puts them in force as they change.
: Keyboard
  `Keyboard:RepeatDelay`, in milliseconds, and `Keyboard:RepeatRate`, repeats a second.
: Mouse
  `Mouse:Speed`, from 1 to 10.
: Deskbar
  `Deskbar:Clock24` and `Deskbar:Gauges`.
: Grants
  The grants recorded at radharc(4)'s trusted prompt, each as its app, its service and its answer, Allowed or Refused.

A setting shows its label and its control: − and + for a number, stepping 50 for a range wider than 300 and 1 otherwise, and stopping at the range's ends; On or Off for a switch; a button a choice for a choice, the chosen one marked.
A change is written to `/data/Settings/<area>` at once.
Defaults sets each of the area's settings to its default, and Revert to what it was when the window opened.
In Grants, Revoke removes a recorded grant, so the app is asked again the next time; Grants has no Defaults or Revert.

A change made elsewhere, by rc's `attr` or another app, is shown as it is made: a thread waits on a watch of `/data/Settings` and wakes the window only for a change to its area.
Nothing else wakes it.
Tab moves between the controls and Space or Enter presses one; Control-W closes the window, and the program ends.

Keyboard's manifest; the others differ in the area and the name:

```text
service prefs-keyboard
program preferences
env PREFS_AREA=Keyboard
app Keyboard
preferences
export
use windows
mount /data fs/volume
mount /lib/fonts bootfs/lib/fonts
```

# EXAMPLES

Open Keyboard's preferences:

```rc
echo start prefs-keyboard >/svc/launcher/ctl
```

# FILES

: `/svc/prefs-<area>/status`
  Read only, a line each: `area <name>`; `ready` once drawn; `<setting> <value>` for each setting shown, or `grant <app>.<service> allowed|refused` for each recorded grant; and `wakeups <n>`, how many times its loop has woken.
: `/data/Settings/<area>`
  The area's settings (settings(2)).

# ENVIRONMENT

: `PREFS_AREA`
  The area: `Appearance`, `Keyboard`, `Mouse`, `Deskbar` or `Grants`.
: `PREFS_TEST`
  Set, it sets the area's settings to their defaults at start and logs each line of `status` that changes.

